  "conclusion": "The donors expose at least two protection geometries. The alpha 7S III 2.15 and 3.01 pair precisely places the usable decryption boundary after the shared UDTRFIRM first stage and before the camera-resident second protected stage. Their nonzero, version-varying 16-byte prefixes and 256-byte suffixes are now fingerprinted without exposing bytes, but those shapes do not prove IV or signature roles, no signature implementation or trust anchor is located, neither donor is fully decrypted, and no installable alpha 6400 artifact exists."
